WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.880
Start incredibly small.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.480
Pick one single team, and one

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.340
recurring high -value decision.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.540
The regional inventory review we discussed

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.739
is a perfect example.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:10.580
Keep it contained.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.940
Connect only the specific data sources

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.639
needed for that one decision.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.740
Define the handful of concepts that

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.880
actually change the answer.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.040
And most importantly, aggressively

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.320
test ambiguous requests and missing

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.340
data scenarios to see exactly how

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.640
the system fails under pressure.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.800
Do not try to boil the

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.100
ocean and map the entire corporation's

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.560
semantic logic on day one.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.740
Exactly. You only expand the scope

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.580
when that first team can complete

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.320
their workflow with dependably accurate

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.460
answers, a highly manageable human

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.580
review burden, and a fully understood,

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.119
predictable operating cost.
